PART C -- A NEW RISK THE LANE ITSELF CREATES: does the clock tachyon come back?
          On FRW the deposited action has NO homogeneous source for phi -- which is exactly why Q_0 = 0
          is an exact solution and the tachyon is cured.  Any DIRECT MATTER coupling supplies one.
==========================================================================================================================
  
  C1  L49 P1 reproduced independently: the clock's induced gradient-mass coefficient is K2*Qbar**2/a**2,
      i.e. exactly K_2 Qbar^2 / a^2 -- tachyonic at K_2 = -|K_2| and vanishing IDENTICALLY at Qbar = 0.
  [PASS] C1 [control] the clock tachyon's coefficient is exactly K_2 Qbar^2/a^2, reproducing L49 P1 with independent code -- so any mechanism that forces Qbar away from zero revives it   (coefficient of (dT/dx)^2 = K2*Qbar**2/a**2, zero at Qbar = 0)
  
  C2  On an exactly homogeneous slice: J^mu = n^nu grad_nu n^mu = 0 (the comoving congruence is
      geodesic) and Y = q^ab d_a phi d_b phi = 0 (no spatial gradients).  So in the DEPOSITED action the
      phi equation on FRW is d/dt[a^3 K'(Qbar)] = 0, which admits Qbar = 0 exactly -- the cure.
      A direct coupling  -8 pi G (2 - K_B) phi rho_s  supplies a homogeneous source that does not vanish:
          d/dt[a^3 K'(Qbar)] = -8 pi G (2 - K_B) rho_s a^3   =>   Qbar = -4 pi G (2-K_B) rhobar_s t / |K_2|
  [PASS] C2 the forced condensate is solved rather than asserted: a^3 Qbar = C t solves the sourced clock equation exactly for a constant comoving source density   (d/dt(a^3 Qbar)/a^3 = C/a(t)**3 = C/a^3, which is the constant comoving source rho_s a^3 divided by a^3 -- so Qbar is NOT zero once any matter couples directly to phi, and by C1 the clock tachyon is revived)
  
  C3  In matter domination Qbar = -H f_s (2 - K_B)/|K_2| with f_s = rho_s/rho_total, so the induced
      condensate carries Omega_K = f_s^2 (2-K_B)^2/(6|K_2|), and ON THE CLOSURE LOCUS c_2|K_2| = (2-K_B)^2
      BOTH |K_2| AND (2-K_B) CANCEL:   Omega_K = f_s^2 c_2/6,   rate/H = f_s sqrt(c_2/2c_14) = f_s sqrt(sigma/2).
      The exhibited point has c_2 = 1.6793e-06, |K_2| = 1.9294e+06, sigma = 1.679313, c_14 = 1.0e-06.
        V-A, source = baryons  : f_s = Omega_b/Omega_m = 0.1556  ->  Omega_K = 6.773e-09, rate/H = 0.1425
        V-B, source = the cold : f_s = Omega_c/Omega_m = 0.8444  ->  Omega_K = 1.996e-07, rate/H = 0.7738
      Stability (the programme's own criterion, L49 P3 / g03w) is rate <= H at every a, i.e. f_s^2 sigma <= 2, i.e. f_s <= sqrt(2/sigma) = 1.0913.
  [PASS] C4 the revived clock condensate does NOT violate the tachyon gate -- and it cannot, for any source, because f_s = rho_s/rho_total <= 1 while the bound is sqrt(2/sigma) > 1 across the whole clock window   (rate/H = 0.143 (V-A, margin 7.0x) and 0.774 (V-B, margin 1.29x); the bound f_s <= sqrt(2/sigma) is 1.091 at sigma* = 1.6793 and 1.063 at the top of the clock window sigma < 1.7716, both above 1, so the gate is structurally safe -- c_14 cancels entirely and the margin is a pure number set by sigma alone. THIS IS A REAL COST NONETHELESS: the deposited theory satisfies the gate IDENTICALLY (Qbar = 0 exactly), and V-B satisfies it with a margin of only 1.29x)
  
  C5  V-B makes the cold particles' mass depend on phi, so Omega_c could drift between recombination and
      today, which would move the CMB window.  The cosmological amplitude is phi ~ Qbar/H = f_c (2-K_B)/|K_2| = 7.88e-07,
      so the fractional mass drift is (2-K_B) phi/2 = 7.09e-07.
  [PASS] C5 the compensating coupling leaves the cold component pressureless and its comoving density constant to better than 1e-5, so the CMB window f = 1.000 +/- 0.010 is unchanged by the modification   (fractional drift 7.09e-07, five orders below the CMB's 1% error on Omega_c h^2; the cold component still scales as a^-3 and the third-peak determination is untouched)

