==========================================================================================================================
PART E -- THE PRICE.  Baryon-sourced modified gravity has known costs; which of them actually bite here?
==========================================================================================================================

  E1  EQUIVALENCE PRINCIPLE.  In BOTH variants the cold component and the baryons no longer fall
      identically: baryons feel the MOND kernel and the cold component does not. At f = 0.582 the
      median fractional difference across SPARC is eta = kernel/total = 0.391, i.e. an O(1) violation
      BETWEEN SECTORS. Two things it is NOT:
        (i) it is not a violation within the Standard Model. In V-B baryons stay minimally coupled to g,
            so there is NO composition dependence and MICROSCOPE/Eotvos are untouched. In V-A the
            conformal coupling is to the TRACE T_b, so electromagnetic binding energy (traceless)
            decouples and a composition dependence DOES appear -- one more reason V-B is the variant to
            carry;
        (ii) it is not inconsistent with the LambdaCDM halo used throughout. In V-B the cold component
            feels only the Newtonian field of rho_b + rho_c, which is exactly the gravity under which
            abundance-matched NFW halos are built -- so the halo library is self-consistent, and MORE
            so than under total sourcing, where the halo would itself have been MOND-boosted.
  [PASS] E1 the equivalence-principle cost is confined to the DARK sector and does not touch any laboratory or Solar-System test   (in V-B it is: baryons and photons remain minimally coupled to the single metric g (the programme's own requirement I2), so gamma_PPN, Eotvos and MICROSCOPE are untouched, and the violation is between the visible and dark sectors alone, where it is unobservable except through the halo's equilibrium -- which is the LambdaCDM one by construction. Magnitude eta = 0.39 (median across SPARC). In V-A it is NOT confined: the conformal coupling to T_b is composition-dependent through the traceless electromagnetic binding energy)

  E2  LENSING, and this is where the two variants part company.
      In V-A the drag coupling is DELETED, so the only thing the MOND sector contributes to the Einstein
      equation is its own gradient energy. Deep-MOND AQUAL has energy density ~ |grad phi|^3/(8 pi G a_0),
      against a phantom density ~ |grad phi|/(4 pi G r); the ratio is |grad phi|^2 r/(2 a_0 c^2) =
      1.61e-07 at 10 kpc in a galaxy and 1.61e-05 at 1 Mpc in a cluster. The phantom therefore
      does not gravitate: light is deflected by the baryons and the cold component ONLY.
      and that is not a modelling choice. Derived here rather than quoted: for a generic static isotropic
      metric g = diag(-N^2, B^2, B^2, B^2) with arbitrary N(x), B(x), and a conformal rescaling
      gtilde = A(x)^2 g, the Christoffel difference contracted on a vector k that is NULL with respect to
      g satisfies  D^mu k^nu - D^nu k^mu = 0 for every mu, nu -- i.e. the extra acceleration is PARALLEL
      to k, so the null curve is unchanged up to reparametrisation. A conformally coupled scalar cannot
      bend light, whatever it does to matter.  (This is why TeVeS carries a DISFORMAL matter metric and a
      vector, and why AeST couples its scalar to the aether's acceleration instead of to matter: both
      couplings are UNIVERSAL, which is what buys the equivalence principle and lensing at once.)
  [FAIL] E2 a conformally baryon-coupled MOND scalar still lenses   (it does not, and this is derived rather than asserted: with a generic static isotropic metric and an arbitrary conformal factor, the connection difference contracted on a g-null k comes out parallel to k (all sixteen antisymmetric combinations vanish identically), so null geodesics are unchanged. Combined with the energy-density ratio (1.6e-07 in a galaxy, 1.6e-05 in a cluster) this says V-A predicts M_dyn/M_lens > 1 by the FULL phantom -- the failure mode that the repository's own record puts at 21.2 sigma for the un-completed kernel and that the AeST drag coupling cures to 0.601 sigma)
  
  E3  how badly does V-A's lensing failure bite ONCE the cold component is present? At f = 0.569:
        clusters: M_dyn/M_lens = (1 + 3.09 + 2.64)/(1 + 3.09) = 1.646, against the observed 1.0-1.3;
