==========================================================================================================================
THREE-SENTENCE VERDICT
==========================================================================================================================
  Baryon sourcing is a legitimate action-level modification and it survives the test that could have killed it
  outright -- conservation and the Bianchi identity are untouched, because the change is made in the Lagrangian and
  diffeomorphism invariance then guarantees grad_mu T^mu_nu(total) = 0, with only the individually coupled species
  exchanging energy with the scalar -- and in the variant that keeps the drag coupling (V-B) it also keeps lensing =
  dynamics, the preferred-frame parameters, c_T = c and the mode count, at the cost of one chosen coefficient, an
  O(1) equivalence-principle violation confined to the dark sector, and a clock-tachyon margin that falls from
  IDENTICAL to 1.29x.

  It moves both of the windows it was supposed to move: the galaxy ceiling rises from f <= 0.355 / 0.276 to 0.582 /
  0.486 and the cluster requirement rises from 0.316 +/- 0.100 / 0.261 +/- 0.093 to 0.569 +/- 0.130 / 0.508 +/-
  0.133, so that galaxies and clusters now agree to 0.1 sigma at f ~ 0.57 -- but the CMB does not move at all, and
  the intersection stays EMPTY with the gap narrowed from 2.8x to 1.7x (canonical) and 3.6x to 2.1x (alt).

  What closes it is a theorem, not a number: the CMB window cannot move because on the closure locus the MOND sector
  contributes exactly zero to linear growth, so re-sourcing a field that contributes nothing changes nothing; and
  the galaxy window cannot reach f = 1 because at that abundance the LambdaCDM halo alone already reproduces SPARC
  to 0.171 dex, leaving no room for the kernel evaluated on the baryons -- which is 74% of the overshoot, is the
  MOND anomaly itself, and is the one thing re-sourcing cannot touch. The only remaining move is to suppress the
  kernel where the cold component dominates (s <= 0.495 at f = 1), which is L49's option (b) and a different lane.

  CAVEATS, stated rather than buried:
   (i)   nothing here favours this framework over LambdaCDM and nothing here constrains LambdaCDM. The
         cold component and its abundance-matched profile are LambdaCDM's, imported wholesale; the
         stellar-to-halo-mass relation remains a free function of host mass (L49 M5).
   (ii)  f_gal is the GENEROUS criterion (median RAR shift inside the RAR's own 0.11 dex), carried so the
         candidate is not handed a manufactured deficit. The strict criterion gives 0.375 / 0.270, on which
         even the galaxy-cluster overlap closes. The full table at nine values of f is printed.
   (iii) abundance matching carries ~0.30 dex of systematic on log M200; it moves f_gal and the cluster
         requirement together and cannot close a gap of 1.7x.
   (iv)  V-B's compensating coefficient is fixed by one condition but chosen rather than forced by a
         symmetry (B3). Whether the SAME coefficient also exactly cancels the MOND force on the cold
         component is a weak-field question this lane does not settle; it does not affect any number here,
         because every window is computed from what BARYONS and LIGHT feel, and it would only alter the
         cold component's own equilibrium profile -- for which the LambdaCDM library is already assumed.
   (v)   the induced-condensate calculation is matter-domination scaling on a flat FRW background,
         calibrated against g03w's published rate through the same formula L49 X5 uses. It fixes the
         STRUCTURE (rate/H = f_s sqrt(sigma/2), with c_14 and |K_2| cancelling on the closure locus); it is
         not a full cosmological-perturbation calculation.
   (vi)  E3's cluster significance for V-A rests on 5-cluster weak-lensing noise and is NOT a kill on its
         own; the load-bearing statement there is structural (a conformal coupling cannot bend light).

